      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (some references say 2,000 to 3,000 mg/day). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity goes up, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose.** If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying it was intentionally confirmed.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
